      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Percutaneous revascularization of thrombus containing saphenous vein grafts is associated with a high incidence of acute complications. This case report describes successful revascularization of an occluded vein graft employing angioscopically guided sequential urokinase infusion, TEC atherectomy and stent implantation."},
